<RickenbackerGuideLayout title="Rickenbacker Finish Colors And Dating" metaTitle="Rickenbacker Finish Colors: Fireglo, Mapleglo And Jetglo" description="Identify Rickenbacker Fireglo, Mapleglo and Jetglo finishes. Compare colors, finish wear and period details with photographs of guitars from my archive." canonical="/rickenbacker-finish-colors/">
 <section class="rk-hero"><div class="rk-wrap"><p class="rk-lede">Identify Mapleglo, Fireglo, Jetglo and other finish names, and learn what color can tell you about a Rickenbacker’s age and originality.</p><p class="rk-byline">Updated October 15, 2026</p><nav class="rk-toc" aria-label="On this page">{topics.map(t=><a href={'#'+t.id}>{t.title}</a>)}</nav><a href="/rickenbacker-serial-numbers/">Back To The Rickenbacker Serial Lookup</a></div></section>
 <section class="rk-section"><div class="rk-wrap rk-article"><div class="rk-note"><strong>Check The Serial And The Model Together</strong><p>Dates below describe common production periods. Parts overlap between models, and reissues or replacements can resemble earlier hardware. Use several details before deciding that a part conflicts with the serial.</p></div><div class="rk-photo-grid jvg-img2"><RickenbackerPhoto file="images/rickenbacker-serial/1960s-rickenbacker-360-2-scaled.jpg" alt="Natural Mapleglo Rickenbacker 360" caption="Mapleglo leaves the maple grain visible. Clear finish can become warmer in color as it ages." /><RickenbackerPhoto file="images/1968-rickenbacker-4005-azureglo-scaled.jpg" alt="Blue Azureglo 1968 Rickenbacker 4005" caption="Joe’s 1968 4005 in Azureglo. A dated example illustrates the color without establishing the date of another blue instrument." /></div><div class="rk-photo-grid jvg-img2"><RickenbackerPhoto file="images/rickenbacker-dating/360-12-fireglo-finish.jpg" alt="Red Fireglo sunburst fading to a light center on a Rickenbacker 360/12" caption="Fireglo on a 360/12: red edges fade into a lighter center, with the maple grain showing through. The shade is an example, not a year code." /><RickenbackerPhoto file="images/rickenbacker-dating/jetglo-bass-finish.jpg" alt="Opaque black Jetglo finish on a bound Rickenbacker bass" caption="Jetglo is the black finish shown on this bass. Judge the body color separately from its installed pickguard and hardware." /></div><h2 id="jvg-s-41-finishes">Finishes</h2><p>Use the <a href="/rickenbacker-serial-numbers/#decoder">Rickenbacker serial lookup</a> to check the date before comparing color. Finish names describe appearance, and the same name can occur across different models and periods.</p>
      <div class="timeline">
        <div class="tl-item"><span class="tl-date">1956 to 1959</span><span class="tl-desc"><strong>Yellow-to-brown sunburst.</strong> The original Rickenbacker sunburst, sometimes called “autumnglo” before that name was formalized.</span></div>
        <div class="tl-item"><span class="tl-date">1958 to Present</span><span class="tl-desc"><strong>Mapleglo</strong>, a clear natural finish that shows the wood. Available from 1958 onward.</span></div>
        <div class="tl-item"><span class="tl-date">1960 to Present</span><span class="tl-desc"><strong>Fireglo</strong>, yellow-to-red sunburst. The red sunburst varies in shade and coverage. Replaces the earlier yellow-to-brown version.</span></div>
        <div class="tl-item"><span class="tl-date">1960 to 1980</span><span class="tl-desc"><strong>Autumnglo</strong>, red-to-brown sunburst. Discontinued approximately 1980.</span></div>
        <div class="tl-item"><span class="tl-date">1984 to ~1996</span><span class="tl-desc"><strong>Jetglo (black) with Black Hardware/Black Trim (BH/BT):</strong> All-black hardware era coincides with the paddle headstock introduction and later the <a href="/rickenbacker-tuner-dating-guide/#jvg-s-27-schaller-m6-mini-m6-to-1985-to-1996">Schaller tuner transition</a>.</span></div>
      </div>

      <h2 id="finish-names">Common Finish Names</h2><div class="rk-table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Scrollable Rickenbacker Reference Table" tabindex="0"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Appearance</th><th scope="col">Dating Limit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Mapleglo</td><td>Natural maple under clear finish</td><td>Long-running finish; yellowing does not establish a year.</td></tr><tr><td>Fireglo</td><td>Red sunburst with a lighter center</td><td>Shade varies across periods and instruments.</td></tr><tr><td>Jetglo</td><td>Black</td><td>The name describes the body finish, not necessarily black hardware.</td></tr><tr><td>Azureglo</td><td>Blue</td><td>Compare a dated example and verify the serial and originality.</td></tr><tr><td>Autumnglo</td><td>Brown-toned sunburst</td><td>Compare sheen and period specifications; names and finish treatments vary.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2 id="finish-originality">Checking Finish Originality</h2><p>Photograph the front, back, neck and headstock in indirect daylight. Include worn edges and any chips already present. Different lighting, camera settings and clear-coat aging can make the same finish look different in two photographs.</p><p>Look for finish over binding, filled holes, abrupt color changes around hardware and wear that stops at a repair. Compare the <a href="/rickenbacker-tailpiece-dating-guide/#bridges-and-replacement-evidence">bridge and tailpiece mounting footprints</a> when checking those areas. These are reasons for closer inspection, not proof of a refinish. Leave the instrument assembled for a <a href="/free-appraisal/rickenbacker/">Rickenbacker appraisal from photos</a>.</p><p>Color names recur, and custom orders and later recreations complicate a date estimate. A familiar vintage color on a newer serial can be factory correct. Check <a href="/rickenbacker-body-binding-and-inlays/">body shape, binding and inlays</a> and <a href="/rickenbacker-knobs-and-controls/">knobs and controls</a> alongside the finish.</p><h2>Get Help Identifying Your Rickenbacker</h2><p>Send photos of the complete instrument, serial plate and the detail you want checked. Include any known repair or replacement history.</p><p><a class="rk-button" href="/free-appraisal/rickenbacker/">Get A Free Rickenbacker Appraisal</a></p><p>Continue with <a href="/rickenbacker-body-binding-and-inlays/">Rickenbacker body, binding and inlay details</a> or return to <a href="/rickenbacker-serial-numbers/">the serial lookup and dating charts</a>.</p></div></section>
